@* L3 break-glass. A LOOPBACK request keeps Settings even under enforced RBAC, so a bad
   configuration (rotated OAuth secret, unreachable domain, hand-edited rbac-config.json)
   is recoverable from the console instead of by deleting Config\rbac-users.json on disk.
   Scoped to this page and Onboarding — the "settings" permission also gates
   /service-management, /audit-log and the report-bundle owner editor, and break-glass must
   not reach those. See AppUserState.IsAuthorizedWithBreakGlass. *@
@if (!UserState.IsAuthorizedWithBreakGlass("settings"))
{
    <div style="padding: 32px;">
        <AccessDenied RequiredRole="Admin" Message="Settings are restricted to Admin users." />
    </div>
    return;
}
else if (UserState.IsLoopback && !UserState.IsAuthorized("settings"))
{
    <div class="rbac-breakglass-banner" style="margin:16px 24px 0;padding:12px 16px;border:1px solid #c93;border-radius:6px;background:rgba(204,153,51,0.12)">
        <strong>Recovery access.</strong> You are signed in as
        <em>@(UserState.IsAuthenticated ? UserState.DisplayName : "an unauthenticated local user")</em>,
        which does not have the Admin role — this page is open because you are connected from
        this machine. Fix the RBAC configuration below, then sign in normally.
    </div>
}

@* The enforcement posture, rendered above the tabs rather than inside "Security & Access",
   because the operator has no reason to open that tab — the whole point is that nothing they did
   caused this. Enforcement can fall away with no operator action at all (a half-written
   rbac-users.json, a disabled provider, an OAuth secret that expired), and until 2026-08-03 the
   only place it showed was the `enforced` field of /auth/me.

   EVERY WORD BELOW IS COMPUTED. This block used to hard-code its headline — a sentence asserting
   that access control was switched on and unenforced — and render it whenever the lapse list was
   non-empty. Driven across all seven damaged-config shapes, every one gave Enabled=false with
   lapse.Count=1, so the banner rendered and claimed a switch position that had never been read,
   while the log branched on the same fact and correctly reported that the file had not loaded.
   One register: the sentence AND the decision to show it both come from
   RbacService.DescribeEnforcementPosture, which is the same object the log writes.

   Do not put a literal claim about enforcement in this markup — not in the banner, not in a
   comment. RbacRound15RegressionTests reads this file and fails on one, deliberately: a claim
   nobody can distinguish from a rendered string is how the last seven rounds each shipped a
   sentence that outran its evidence. *@
@if (EnforcementPosture.IsProblem)
{
    <div class="rbac-lapse-banner" role="alert"
         style="margin:16px 24px 0;padding:12px 16px;border:1px solid var(--error,#e05252);border-radius:6px;background:rgba(224,82,82,0.12)">
        <strong>@EnforcementPosture.Headline</strong>
        @EnforcementPosture.Detail
        <ul style="margin:6px 0 0;padding-left:20px;">
            @foreach (var reason in EnforcementPosture.Reasons)
            {
                <li style="font-size:12px;">@reason</li>
            }
        </ul>
    </div>
}

<div class="settings-page">
    <h2>Settings</h2>

    <div class="settings-layout">
        <nav class="settings-rail" aria-label="Settings sections">
            @if (BuildModules.Premium)
            {
                <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="@(_activeTab == "Full Audit" ? "active" : "")" @onclick='() => SetActiveTab("Full Audit")'>Full Audit</a>
            }
            <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="@(_activeTab == "General" ? "active" : "")" @onclick='() => SetActiveTab("General")'>General</a>
            <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="@(_activeTab == "Performance" ? "active" : "")" @onclick='() => SetActiveTab("Performance")'>Performance</a>
            <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="@(_activeTab == "Diagnostics" ? "active" : "")" @onclick='() => SetActiveTab("Diagnostics")'>Diagnostics</a>
            <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="@(_activeTab == "Security & Access" ? "active" : "")" @onclick='() => SetActiveTab("Security & Access")'>Security & Access</a>
            <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="@(_activeTab == "Integrations" ? "active" : "")" @onclick='() => SetActiveTab("Integrations")'>Integrations</a>
            <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="@(_activeTab == "Compliance" ? "active" : "")" @onclick='() => SetActiveTab("Compliance")'>Compliance</a>
        </nav>

        <div class="settings-content" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; max-width: 800px;">

            @* ── Full Audit management (full builds only; card is a never-ship component) ── *@
            @if (BuildModules.Premium && _activeTab == "Full Audit")
            {
                <div class="settings-group" id="set-full-audit">
                    <ActivateFullAuditCard />
                </div>
            }

